  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MOL: Innovate Moldova: Strengthen Moldova&#x2019;s innovation ecosystem and business resilience for sustainable growth</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Moldova is contending with war-related shocks, energy price volatility, and inflation while fast-tracking alignment with the European Union acquis. These pressures expose structural weaknesses: an innovation ecosystem that is still maturing, firms with limited capacity to meet EU standards and trade digitally, growing cyber risks, and uneven uptake of trusted digital public services. The suspension of USAID support to the former Future Technologies Activity created financing gaps just as key reforms and assets&#x2014;media and ICT skills pipelines, e-commerce regulation and firm adoption, cybersecurity training, and business-facing modules of the EVO application&#x2014;needed consolidation and scale. Innovate Moldova maintains momentum, but several high impact workstreams remain underfunded, risking loss of earlier UK/FTA gains and slowing EU market integration. The objective of this project is to close these gaps rapidly through a focused UK add-on delivered inside Innovate Moldova&#x2019;s architecture: strengthen institutions and service delivery (centres, BSOs, associations, EVO), raise firm competitiveness and export readiness (e-commerce, certifications, promotion), and build cyber resilience and skills (basic and advanced courses). This directly addresses the identified problems and advances Good Governance Fund outcomes on accountable reform, inclusive economic resilience, and resilience to hostile threats, with strong engagement of civil society and the private sector.</narrative>
  </description>
